{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774127733,"nonce":"Qi+yWlCd6d+3ebHJMueO2i1xI8s=","title":"Umbrella: Two-mode architecture — SDK + Channel as equal session modes","message":"Umbrella issue for the architectural change to make SDK and Channel equal-status session modes in Mandible Console.\n\n## Vision\nTwo equal modes for Claude sessions:\n1. **SDK Mode** — Mandible spawns Claude via Agent SDK. API key required. Full control.\n2. **Channel Mode** — Mandible launches Claude CLI with --channels server:mandible. User OAuth. Zero-config default.\n\n## Child issues\n- ca3d052: Channel mode terminal view (xterm.js for channel sessions)\n- 2a9cf71: Dynamic preset switching (mid-conversation, SDK-only)\n- 83b498e: Hybrid SDK+Channel injection\n- 71ca935: Console session creation: SDK vs Channel mode selector\n\n## Related closed issues\n- 73e0adf: MCP channel server\n- 11d23eb: External CLI as first-class tier\n- ef4eb11: PTY deprecation plan\n- 0b454df: External CLI first-class support\n\n## Key design decisions\n- Channel mode re-legitimizes PTY as terminal transport (PTY carries I/O, channel carries structured events)\n- Preset interaction differs by mode: SDK=per-query, Channel=per-session\n- Permission handling differs: SDK=PermissionAwareBackend, Channel=terminal interaction\n- Fork/resume differs: SDK=message-level, Channel=session-level","files":null}]}